  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal setup using multiprofile data with avgpool aggregation, achieving validation accuracy of 0.6186 and F1 of 0.6103, higher than singleprofile multimodal baselines (0.5266 accuracy). The results suggest multiprofile data may improve performance, but the role of avgpool aggregation remains uncertain without direct comparison to other aggregation methods. The improvement over singleprofile benchmarks indicates potential benefits of multiprofile settings, though further experiments are needed to isolate design choices."
